  "description": "The local cache: AES-256-GCM with a key derived from the device fingerprint. A cache file copied to another computer does not decrypt there, which is what makes an offline licence non-transferable.",
  "notes": [
    "HKDF-SHA256 over the fingerprint string, not over a stored key. There is nothing to steal from the file system.",
    "The product slug goes into both the HKDF info and the additional authenticated data, so a cache from one product cannot be replayed into another on the same machine.",
    "The nonce is random in production; these vectors pin a fixed one so the ciphertext is reproducible.",
    "A cache that fails to decrypt is discarded, never fatal. Corruption happens - a full disk, a killed process - and the right answer is to ask the server again, not to refuse to start."
